From e32d81de71f86b0f22713db8ec308bd1543a6934 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:19:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] perf(algorithm): bm_fft compares FFT kernels and plans
 per size and prints this host's route table

Every (type, N) is one interleaved comparison group: `SimdFFT` (reference), `StockhamFFT` with its default and alternative radix plans, the dispatcher `FFT`, each accuracy-checked against a long-double DFT before timing, in `hot` (one frame) and `stream` (frames cycling through 2^16 points) modes.
Before the tables the run prints the `FFTRoutes.hpp` tables this host would choose: a candidate replaces the current route only when its paired ratio's 95 % interval lies entirely below.
Benchmarks keep `-march=native` unless the configuration already sets `-march`, so one host can measure every vector width it supports.

```bash
cmake -DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS=-march=x86-64-v3 ...   # 256-bit table on an AVX-512 host
taskset -c 2 env BM_FFT_ROUNDS=40 BM_FFT_MAX_LOG2=20 BM_FFT_MIN_SAMPLE_MS=5 ./bm_fft
```

### Changes
- `bm_fft.cpp`: rewritten on `benchmark::compare`; `BM_FFT_ROUNDS`, `BM_FFT_MAX_LOG2`, `BM_FFT_MIN_SAMPLE_MS`; header line with compiler, simd backend, width and CPU
- `algorithm/benchmarks/CMakeLists.txt`, `bench/CMakeLists.txt`: a configured `-march` wins over `-march=native`
